#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# clamp

#% text
# `clamp(x, lo, hi)` gives `x` limited to the interval from `lo` to `hi`: `lo` when `x < lo`, `hi` when `x > hi`, else `x`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
clamp(5, 0, 3)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
clamp(-2, 0, 3)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
clamp(1.5, 0, 3)
#% output
#= 1.5

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Exact numbers stay exact:

#% cell
clamp(7/2, 0, 3)
#% output
#= 3

#% text
# Apply it to each element of a list:

#% cell
map(x => clamp(x, 0, 1), [-1, 0.5, 2])
#% output
#= [0, 0.5, 1]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `min`, `max`, `rescale`
